{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }({x}^{5}+4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-35122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We identify the leading term and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }({x}^{5}+4) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }({x}^{5}) \\\\  & =-\\infty \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-35122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-35122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-35122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\infty "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-35122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-113928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-113928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-113928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-113928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-113928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "{tan}^{2}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-113928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-92997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=5(7)^{x}-35.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-92997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n5(7)^{x}-35=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding $35$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(7)^{x}-35 & =0 \\\\ 5(7)^{x}-\\cancel{35}+\\cancel{35} & =0+35 \\\\ 5(7)^{x} & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(7)^{x} & =35 \\\\ {7}^{x} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(7)$, we equate the exponents. This gives\n\n$$\nx=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-92997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-92997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-92997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-92997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-61906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/assets/586b2c9d3409b68436f16715937b7a4bf0abdf8c1a05c628ccafdc49cf6d641d.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the cube above if it is $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $4\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $4\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-61906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/assets/2c8a118f8f3c3ccba67e25ae09096ef1ec0cf15fc6a5e7f9de68f797b7105c80.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares only.\n\nThe squares are $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $4\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=4\\times 4=16\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the cube consists of $6$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =6\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =6\\times 16 \\\\  & =96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-61906" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-61906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-61906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "112\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "128\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "64\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "80\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-61906" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "96\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-103844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=7$ for some $x$, then find the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+12\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-103844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+12\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+12\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=7,$ then $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+12\\pi )=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-103844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-103844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-103844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "19"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-103844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-88454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{3x}-25\\cdot {4}^{3x}=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-88454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{3x}-25\\cdot {4}^{3x} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-25)\\cdot {4}^{3x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-25=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{4}^{3x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-25=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+5)(x-5)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-5,5.$\n\n- The equation ${4}^{3x}=0$ has no solutions because ${4}^{3x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-5,5,$ and their product is $(-5)\\cdot 5=-25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-88454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-88454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-88454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-25"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-88454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-25"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-102416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[7]{3x+13}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-102416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[7]{3x+13}-1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[7]{3x+13}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{3x+13} & =1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[7]{3x+13})^{7} & ={1}^{7} \\\\ 3x+13 & =1 \\\\ 3x & =-12 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-102416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-102416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-102416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-4"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{13}{3}"] ["math" "x=4"] ["math" "x=\\frac{4}{3}"] ["text" "The function has no roots"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-102416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-313365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{x+3},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | ${(x+3)}^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-313365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=(x+1)^{2}$ and the denominator $v(x)=x+3.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2(x+1),\\,{v}^{′}(x)=1.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)\\cdot (x+3)-(x+1)^{2}\\cdot 1}{(x+3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)[2(x+3)-(x+1)]}{{(x+3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)[2x+6-x-1]}{{(x+3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)(x+5)}{{(x+3)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-313365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-313365" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-313365" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x^2+6x+5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-340945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}$ at the point $(2,2).$\n\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-340945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-16{x}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,2):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(2)=-\\frac{16}{(2)^{3}}=-\\frac{16}{8}=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{-2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2) \\\\ 2y-4 & =x-2 \\\\ x-2\\cdot y & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-340945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-340945" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-340945" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-340945" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-340945" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-19050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $a=⟨0,0,0⟩$ and $b=i-j-k$, then $a-2b=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-19050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that\n\n$$\nb=i-j-k=⟨1,-1,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nTo compute $a-2b,$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-2b & =⟨0,0,0⟩-2\\cdot ⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩-⟨2\\cdot 1,2\\cdot (-1),2\\cdot (-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩-⟨2,-2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,2⟩ \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-19050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8096c7f0992d3479ee37d7d62e0922ff5e63de19754b49d049dfbce13dd5fbe7"} {"question" "q-19050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-19050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003941/state.json" "file_sha256" "5ba9e0bb026bdd36572578584e0bf7e6f7f802f6fbf07c0ce9b1f799a2b6e0cf"} {"question" "q-19050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 